[Nx Cloud CI](/docs/features/ci-features#run-ci-on-nx-cloud) reads a `.nx/pipelines/ci.yaml` file that looks like a GitHub Actions workflow, and most step-level syntax carries over.
This guide converts a workflow, then lists how each GitHub Actions key, name, and file maps.

## Convert a workflow

This workflow:

```yaml
# .github/workflows/ci.yml
name: CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  main:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    env:
      NX_CLOUD_ACCESS_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.NX_CLOUD_ACCESS_TOKEN }}
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v7
        with:
          fetch-depth: 0
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v6
        with:
          node-version: 24
          cache: npm
      - run: npm ci
      - uses: nrwl/nx-set-shas@v5
      - run: npx nx-cloud start-workers
      - run: npx nx affected -t lint test build
      - run: npx nx fix-ci
        if: always()
```

Becomes this file:

```yaml
# .nx/pipelines/ci.yaml
name: CI

on:
  main-pushes:
    event: PUSH
    branches: [main]
  pull-requests:
    event: PR
    branches: [main]

jobs:
  main:
    runs-on: linux-medium-js
    workers: 3 linux-large-js
    steps:
      - run: npx nx affected -t lint test build
```

Drop `NX_CLOUD_ACCESS_TOKEN` from `env`.
Nx Cloud CI sets it for you, and a value from a GitHub secret overrides the token of the run, usually with an empty value.

Required status checks need updating, because the check names change to `<name> / <job>`.

## How keys map

| GitHub Actions                                                   | Nx Cloud CI                                                        |
| ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| `on: push` and `on: pull_request`                                | Named triggers with `event: PUSH` or `event: PR`                   |
| `runs-on: ubuntu-latest`                                         | A [launch template](/docs/kb/launch-templates)                     |
| `actions/checkout`, `actions/setup-node`, `npm ci`               | `init-steps` of the launch template                                |
| `nrwl/nx-set-shas`                                               | Automatic                                                          |
| `start-workers`                                                  | `workers` on the job                                               |
| `nx fix-ci`                                                      | Automatic                                                          |
| `uses: owner/repo@ref`                                           | `uses` with a [step template](/docs/kb/custom-steps)               |
| `needs`, `if`, `env`, `timeout-minutes`                          | Same keys                                                          |
| `${{ secrets.X }}`, `${{ vars.X }}`, `${{ needs.<job>.result }}` | Same [expressions](/docs/reference/nx-cloud/ci-config#expressions) |
| `github.event_name` in a condition                               | Works as written. `nxcloud.event_name` is the Nx Cloud name        |

## GitHub Actions names that keep working

Steps copied from a GitHub Actions workflow don't need renaming.
New files can use the Nx Cloud names:

| Nx Cloud                                                                          | Also works as                                                             |
| --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `nxcloud.*`                                                                       | `github.*`                                                                |
| `secrets.NX_CLOUD_VCS_TOKEN`                                                      | `secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN`                                                    |
| `$NX_CLOUD_OUTPUT`, `$NX_CLOUD_PATH`, `$NX_CLOUD_STATE`, `$NX_CLOUD_STEP_SUMMARY` | `$GITHUB_OUTPUT`, `$GITHUB_PATH`, `$GITHUB_STATE`, `$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY` |
| `$NX_CLOUD_ENV`                                                                   | `$GITHUB_ENV`, which also takes multi-line values (`NAME<<EOF`)           |
| `$NX_CLOUD_SHA`, `$NX_CLOUD_REF`, `$NX_CLOUD_RUNNER_OS`, and the rest             | `$GITHUB_SHA`, `$GITHUB_REF`, `$RUNNER_OS`, and the rest                  |

For every variable and file, see [variables and files in each step](/docs/reference/nx-cloud/ci-config#variables-and-files-in-each-step).
`GITHUB_ACTIONS` and `GITHUB_RUN_ID` aren't set, so tools don't detect the job as running in GitHub Actions.
To check for Nx Cloud CI in a script, read `NX_CLOUD_CI`, which is `true` in every job and worker.

## What doesn't carry over

Pull requests from forks, scheduled runs, `strategy.matrix`, GitHub Marketplace actions, and macOS and Windows machines aren't supported yet.
For the full list, see [current limits](/docs/reference/nx-cloud/ci-config#current-limits).
